# WHAT THE CLIENT LEAVES OUT OF `site/`, declared ONCE and read by both things
# that need it: `desktop/build.rs`, which packs the rest into the binary, and
# `scripts/payload_manifest.py`, which describes it to the update channel.
#
# THE CLIENT IS THE SITE, so this lists exclusions and not inclusions. A list of
# what goes in is a list somebody has to remember to extend: a directory the
# site gained and the list did not (`lib/`, `ocr/`) was a feature the client
# silently lacked, and a script the page loads by address answered with nothing.
# Here a new file ships by default, and a difference has to be written down
# with its reason.
#
# A trailing `/` is a whole tree; `*/name` is that file in any directory below
# the root; anything else is one file. Blank lines and `#` lines are ignored.
#
# AND ONE RULE NO LINE STATES: a directory holding `generation.json` ships only
# the names it lists. The site keeps the PREVIOUS build's content-addressed
# files for a browser still holding a page from before the deploy; the client
# swaps its whole directory at once and has no such page, and the wasm alone
# is 10 MB.

# THE LIVE DATA PLANE — the board is rescored every hour against a release that
# moves on a code change. Inside the payload it would bank a new immortal blob
# each rescore and hand every client a file it replaces before reading it. The
# shell fetches it and keeps it beside the release — docs/DISTRIBUTION.md.
board/
board.meta.json

# CLOUDFLARE'S OWN CONFIGURATION, which the CDN reads and never serves.
_headers
_redirects

# FOR CRAWLERS AND AGENTS, never requested by the page. `*/index.html` is each
# page's prerendered copy (the app draws every page from the root
# `index.html`), `og/` the link-preview cards, `weapons/` the markdown twins.
# The three legal pages are not served from here either way: the site's worker
# fills them, and the shell asks it for them (`protocol::SITE_PAGES`).
*/index.html
og/
weapons/
